Chatbot flows are structured conversation paths that guide users toward specific goals, such as resolving an issue, completing a task, or accessing information. These flows represent the business logic behind how a chatbot interacts with users, ensuring consistency and clarity throughout the conversation. 
Each step in the flow is designed to collect user input, make decisions, and deliver outcomes in a seamless and logical sequence.

Well-designed chatbot flows are essential for providing a positive user experience.
They prevent confusion by ensuring conversations stay organized, minimize frustration by guiding users to their objectives efficiently, and reduce the time spent resolving queries.
Whether it’s answering a customer’s question, booking an appointment, or automating an internal task, effective flows create smoother, more productive interactions.

Flexibility is critical to chatbot flows, especially when adapting to varied user inputs and unexpected changes. With the Rasa Platform, businesses can design flows that handle real-world complexities. 
Using tools like Rasa Studio’s Flow Builder, teams can create flows that adjust dynamically to user behavior.


The CALM (Conversational AI with Language Models) dialogue system makes flow design easier by letting you map out a user's journey without worrying about every possible way they might stray from the path.
CALM automatically handles deviations, so you can focus on helping the user rather than restricting their choices. Using Rasa’s no-code tools, businesses can design flows without requiring extensive developer input, accelerating deployment.
